2. Product vision, goals and boundaries
2.1 Vision
Make high-quality, short-form chess tactics easy to solve on any device. The player sees one position, identifies the best move or sequence, receives progressively more informative hints, then can review the line, share the puzzle, or print a worksheet without creating an account.
2.2 Product promises
1. Free tactical practice: Mate in 1, Mate in 2, Mate in 3, and tactical motifs from beginner to advanced.
2. Useful printing: single puzzles and multi-puzzle worksheets with separate answer keys, A4 and US Letter layouts, and optional QR links.
3. No forced identity: no account, public profile, chat, comments, cloud sync, or subscription in the MVP.
4. Reliable static delivery: no server request is required to validate a move or provide the known solution/hints.
5. Respectful monetisation: ads are separated from board controls and cannot be required for puzzle use.
6. Documented provenance: every puzzle and shipped dependency has a traceable source/licence record.
2.3 MVP non-goals
- Full chess games, matchmaking, real-time multiplayer, live ratings or tournaments.
- Accounts, public leaderboards, chat, profiles, user uploads or user-generated puzzle hosting.
- Arbitrary engine analysis or bundled Stockfish.
- Ads disguised as puzzle controls, forced notification prompts, pop-under triggers on board clicks, or forced redirects.
- Behavioural advertising directed at children.
- Indexing every row in a source database just because SSG can generate the URLs.
- A guarantee that a puzzle has only one correct move unless its validated solution data supports that claim.
