6.7 Google AI Studio implementation requirements
Google AI Studio Build mode can generate and iterate a web application from a natural-language brief, and its documented workflow supports code inspection and GitHub import/sync. Its web builds may include a Node.js server runtime, so do not assume an AI Studio preview is automatically an SSG site. The final repository must pass the static-export and clean-hosting checks in this PRD. [R17]
- Use the separate Chessbitz_Google_AI_Studio_Build_Prompt_v1.1.md as the implementation prompt. It repeats the visual tokens and interaction contracts so they are not left to model invention.
- Final deployment target: static files, with generated puzzle/theme/archive routes and assets available at build time; final output must be deployable to Cloudflare Pages or equivalent static hosting through GitHub Actions.
- No runtime server, database, account system, remote chess engine, Gemini API call, or secret key is needed for solving, hints, local progress, share links or PDF generation.
- Use a chess legality library for moves; never ask an LLM to determine whether a chess move is legal or to invent a solution line.
